// THE C LAUNCHER'S WIN32 RESOURCES, and each row is load-bearing rather than decoration.
//
// ASCII ONLY, on purpose: `windres` reads this file with the locale's code page (not UTF-8) unless told otherwise, so a
// non-ASCII byte in a string here would land in the binary as mojibake on a French or Cyrillic Windows. The engine's own
// launcher carries the accented author name because a .NET resource compiler is told the encoding; this one keeps to the
// printable ASCII range and loses nothing a reader needs.
//
// The three entries are found through `-I <repository root>`, which `build.bat` passes, so the icon and the manifest are
// THE SAME FILES the C# launcher and the engine use: one statement of each, no copies to drift.

// ── THE MANIFEST: RT_MANIFEST (24), id 1 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Not cosmetic, and it is the one resource whose absence broke 14 suites: it carries the Common-Controls v6 assembly
// dependency and PerMonitorV2 awareness. A host without it registers NO v6 classes, so measured through a launcher
// without one the corpus' UI suites failed with `[CreateWinControl]: CreateWindowEx for 'SysLink' failed: 1407`
// (ERROR_CLASS_NOT_FOUND), a themed control's paint notification never arrived, and `ListView.DeleteColumn` behaved like
// the legacy control. A payload runs as THIS process, so the manifest has to be this process's.
1 24 "app.manifest"

// ── THE ICON: RT_GROUP_ICON (14), id 32512 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 32512 is IDI_APPLICATION, the id .NET's `<ApplicationIcon>` uses and the one `tools/slc-pack.slc --icon` rewrites, so a
// packed exe's icon replaces THIS group instead of adding a second one the shell would ignore. The same icon as the
// engine's exe, so a packaged app and the CLI it stands in for look alike, and a script's form takes its default icon
// from `Environment.ProcessPath`, which in a host is this exe.
32512 ICON "forward.ico"

// ── THE VERSION: RT_VERSION (16), id 1 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// So a packed app and the launcher it came from can be told apart with one right-click. The numbers are the engine's own
// (1.0.0.0, measured from the C# launcher), and the packer overrides them per app with `--version`.
1 VERSIONINFO
FILEVERSION 1,0,0,0
PRODUCTVERSION 1,0,0,0
FILEFLAGSMASK 0x3fL
FILEFLAGS 0x0L
FILEOS 0x40004L
FILETYPE 0x1L
FILESUBTYPE 0x0L
BEGIN
    BLOCK "StringFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        BLOCK "040904b0"
        BEGIN
            VALUE "CompanyName", "ScriptLangCore"
            VALUE "FileDescription", "ScriptLangCore launcher"
            VALUE "FileVersion", "1.0.0.0"
            VALUE "ProductName", "ScriptLangCore"
            VALUE "ProductVersion", "1.0.0.0"
        END
    END
    BLOCK "VarFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        VALUE "Translation", 0x409, 0x4b0
    END
END
